> Can the conversions like {se} be used with {go'i}?
> For example:
> 
> mi prami do .i ku'i mi senpi ledu'u se go'i
> - I love you but I doubt that you love me.

{se} can indeed be used with {go'i}, but go'i carries the expressed
arguments with it unless they are explicitly replaced, so {le se go'i} 
is {do} in your example, not {mi}.

One way to express what you want is {mi prami do i ku'i mi senpi
le du'u do go'i mi}. 

